Subject: [PATCH 11/12] fix(backend): harden legacy proxy server (CORS, body
 limit, logging)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- CORS was wide open (app.use(cors())) so any website could call this API
  from the browser; now restricted to FRONTEND_URL (comma-separated allowed).
- express.json() had no size limit (unbounded body -> memory DoS); capped at
  1mb.
- Removed API key length logging (key material metadata), keeping presence-only
  logs.

Validation: node --check backend/server.js.

